      "trigger": "The 10Y has backed up to ~4.63% — the upper half of the 4.00-4.90% band — on the oil-inflation impulse into June CPI, with the 30Y at ~5.11% but the 10Y still comfortably below its own proven 5% ceiling. The regime that boxes it holds from both sides: a Fed on hold (band 3.50-3.75%, no cuts priced until 2027) anchors against a runaway break through 5%, while sticky inflation (the last PCE at 4.1% / core 3.4%) keeps it from rallying under 4% — exactly the boxed-in tape a range accrual is paid to harvest, and the back-up toward the top of the band widens the coupon-vs-risk edge without yet threatening the ceiling.",
